":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-01-04T10:46:38Z","updated_at":"2015-01-04T10:46:38Z","body":"@nzakas to confirm my understanding of the discussion here, the rule is currently designed to enforce spacing unless both the starting and ending brackets are on separate lines, which is a bug. Instead, when only one bracket is on a separate line, it should enforce spacing only for the other bracket. Is that correct?\n\n``` js\n// Enforced currently and with the proposed change\nvar arr = [1, 2, 3, 4];\n\n// Not enforced currently, nor with the proposed change\nvar arr = [\n    1, 2, 3, 4\n];\n\n// Beginning and end enforced currently\nvar arr = [1, 2, // Only beginning enforced with the proposed change\n    3, 4\n]; // Ending not enforced with the proposed change\n```\n\nThe following four test cases are pulled directly from `tests/lib/rules/space-in-brackets.js`. According to the rule's original design, there should be one error each. Am I reading that this behavior is incorrect, and all four should pass validation?\n\n``` js\n// \"space-in-brackets\": [2, \"never\"]\nvar obj = {foo: bar,\nbaz: qux\n};\n\n// \"space-in-brackets\": [2, \"never\"]\nvar obj = {\nfoo: bar,\nbaz: qux};\n\n// \"space-in-brackets\": [2, \"never\"]\nvar arr = [1,\n2,\n3,\n4\n];\n\n// \"space-in-brackets\": [2, \"never\"]\nvar arr = [\n1,\n2,\n3,\n4];\n```\n\nIf my interpretation is correct, the change seems strange to me. In fact, I find the spacing in the example given to be confusing: the elements of an array expression and object literal are at the same indentation level on adjacent lines, and the divide between the two gets buried in the third line. I think the given snippet could be improved with either of the following changes, both of which validate without altering this rule:\n\n``` js\n_.template(\n    [\n        'Foo: ${ foo }',\n        'Bar: `${ bar }`.'\n    ].join('\\n'),\n    { foo: 'foo', bar: 'bar' }\n);\n\n_.template([\n    'Foo: ${ foo }',\n    'Bar: `${ bar }`.'\n].join('\\n'), {\n    foo: 'foo',\n    bar: 'bar',\n});\n```\n\nAm I misunderstanding? Or is my eye alone in finding those four test cases kind of ugly?\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/68628582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"btmills","id":1709537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDk1Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1709537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills","html_url":"https://github.com/btmills","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":213768661,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MjEzNzY4NjYx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/213768661","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.